.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTRACE_PF 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtrace_pf
.Nd a DTrace provider for the pf packet filter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Li pf:ip:test:entry,finish
.Pp
.Li pf:ip:rules:entry
.br
.Li pf:ip:anchor:enter
.Pp
.Li pf::reason:set
.Pp
.Li pf:state:state:create,insert,transition,remove,free
.br
.Li pf:state:purge:run
.Pp
.Li pf:frag:reassemble,reassemble6:entry
.br
.Li pf:nat:transaddr:entry
.br
.Li pf:nat:af_to:translate
.br
.Li pf:ip,ip6:route_to:entry
.Pp
.Li pf:table:addr:match,update
.br
.Li pf:rule:jail:match,resolve
.br
.Li pf:syncookie:cookie:send,validate
.Pp
.Li pf:log:pflog:packet
.br
.Li pf:pfsync:packet:send,input
.br
.Li pf:pflow:flow:export
.br
.Li pf:queue:packet:delay
.Pp
.Li pf:ioctl:ioctl:entry,return
.br
.Li pf:ioctl:xact:begin,commit,rollback
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm pf
provider instruments
.Xr pf 4 ,
the
.Ox
packet filter.
All probes are statically defined
.Pq Xr SDT 9
and cost nothing when not enabled.
Structure arguments use the types of the
.Ox
.In net/pfvar.h
and are available to D scripts through CTF.
.Ss Packet path
.Bl -tag -width "pf::reason:set"
.It Li pf:ip:test:entry
Fires before
.Fn pf_test
for a packet.
.Fa arg0
is the address family,
.Fa arg1
the direction (1 in, 2 out, 3 forwarded) and
.Fa args[2]
the
.Vt struct ifnet .
.It Li pf:ip:test:finish
Fires after
.Fn pf_test
with
.Fa arg0
the action (0 pass, 1 drop),
.Fa arg1
the direction and
.Fa args[2]
the interface.
.It Li pf:ip:rules:entry
Ruleset evaluation of a packet without matching state;
.Fa args[0]
is the
.Vt struct pf_pdesc .
.It Li pf:ip:anchor:enter
A ruleset (the main ruleset or an anchor) is evaluated;
.Fa args[1]
is the
.Vt struct pf_ruleset .
.It Li pf::reason:set
Every point where pf records a reason code
.Pq Dv PFRES_*
for a drop, a match or a normalisation decision.
.Fa arg0
is the reason,
.Fa arg1
the source file and
.Fa arg2
the line.
The reasons are: 0 match, 1 bad-offset, 2 fragment, 3 short, 4
normalize, 5 memory, 6 bad-timestamp, 7 congestion, 8 ip-option, 9
proto-cksum, 10 state-mismatch, 11 state-insert, 12 state-limit, 13
src-limit, 14 synproxy, 15 translate, 16 no-route.
.It Li pf:frag:reassemble:entry,Li pf:frag:reassemble6:entry
An IPv4 or IPv6 fragment enters reassembly;
.Fa args[0]
is the mbuf and
.Fa arg1
the direction.
.It Li pf:nat:transaddr:entry
A nat-to, rdr-to or binat-to address is selected;
.Fa args[0]
is the rule,
.Fa args[1]
the packet description.
.It Li pf:nat:af_to:translate
A packet is translated between address families (af-to).
.It Li pf:ip:route_to:entry,Li pf:ip6:route_to:entry
route-to, reply-to or dup-to routing of a packet;
.Fa args[1]
is the state.
.El
.Ss States
.Bl -tag -width "pf:state:state:transition"
.It Li pf:state:state:create
A rule creates a state:
.Fa args[0]
packet description,
.Fa args[1]
rule,
.Fa args[2]
anchor rule.
.It Li pf:state:state:insert
A state is inserted into the state table.
.It Li pf:state:state:transition
A TCP peer changes protocol state:
.Fa args[0]
state,
.Fa arg1
peer (0 source, 1 destination),
.Fa arg2
new state.
.It Li pf:state:state:remove,free
A state is unlinked and later freed.
.It Li pf:state:purge:run
A purge pass of expired states with
.Fa arg0
the scan limit.
.El
.Ss Packet delay
.Bl -tag -width "pf:queue:packet:delay"
.It Li pf:queue:packet:delay
A packet has obtained delay storage and is about to be scheduled:
.Fa arg0
is the queue ID,
.Fa arg1
the requested delay in milliseconds, and
.Fa arg2
the interface index.
The probe exposes packet metadata independently of its storage layout.
Its availability does not imply that the native output path supports
.Cm set delay .
.El
.Ss Tables, logging, synchronisation and control
.Bl -tag -width "pf:table:addr:update"
.It Li pf:table:addr:match
An address is looked up in table
.Fa args[0]
.Pq Vt struct pfr_ktable .
.It Li pf:table:addr:update
Table statistics are updated for a packet.
.It Li pf:rule:jail:match
The 5BSD
.Cm jail
rule option of rule
.Fa args[0]
.Pq Vt struct pf_rule
matched a socket of jail ID
.Fa arg1 .
.It Li pf:rule:jail:resolve
Rule
.Fa args[0]
names a jail and was re-resolved after a jail was created, renamed or
removed:
.Fa arg1
is the old jail ID and
.Fa arg2
the new one, -2 for no jail.
.It Li pf:syncookie:cookie:send,validate
A SYN cookie is sent or an ACK is validated against one.
.It Li pf:log:pflog:packet
A packet is logged to a
.Xr pflog 4
interface:
.Fa args[0]
packet description,
.Fa arg1
reason,
.Fa args[2]
matching rule,
.Fa args[3]
anchor rule.
.It Li pf:pfsync:packet:send,input
A
.Xr pfsync 4
packet is sent or received.
.It Li pf:pflow:flow:export
A state is exported as a
.Xr pflow 4
flow record.
.It Li pf:ioctl:ioctl:entry,return
A
.Pa /dev/pf
ioctl:
.Fa arg0
command,
.Fa arg1
per-open unit and, on return,
.Fa arg2
the error.
.It Li pf:ioctl:xact:begin,commit,rollback
A ruleset transaction step for the named anchor.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles/pf-*.d" -compact
.It Pa /usr/share/dtrace/pf-observe
summary of verdicts, latency, reasons, states, NAT, tables, pflog,
pfsync and pflow activity
.It Pa /usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles/pf-*.d
focused profiles: pf-latency, pf-audit, pf-drops, pf-states,
pf-frags, pf-nat, pf-tables, pf-rules, pf-pfsync, pf-queues
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Count drops by reason and source location:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# dtrace -n 'pf::reason:set { @[arg0, stringof(arg1), arg2] = count(); }'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr pflog 4 ,
.Xr pflow 4 ,
.Xr pfsync 4 ,
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
.Xr SDT 9
